{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["We perish — 'and they shall perish from the midst of the assembly' — if so we all perish day by day. How?" "Everyone who comes near, whoever he may be — every man who approaches the Mishkan to guard it, or [approaches] the vessels of the Mishkan together with the Levites, shall die — for the Holy One, blessed be He, had not yet warned them, since ״והזר הקרב יומת״ had not yet been written. Therefore He warns them in this section: ״וזר לא יקרב אליכם״, and ״והזר הקרב יומת״ — that from here onward they shall not come near at all and shall not die. For even in the section 'Speak to the priests,' where it is written: ״דבר אל אהרן לאמר איש מזרעך אשר יהיה בו מום לא יגש להקריב לחם ה׳״ — there He disqualified only those with blemishes, but strangers He did not disqualify. And what He disqualified there in the section ״אמור אליהם כל איש אשר יקרב״ and so on — that concerns disqualification by bodily impurity, but for the service of strangers in the Mishkan and its vessels we have not yet seen a death penalty."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:30.233977764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}